PRETABLE -- #530 (lcaisalane) kill table 4, CLOSING PASS 2's REPAIR 3 (93 rows).  Written BEFORE the table runs, and
before HEAD_r4 / FIX_r4 (the 93-row instrument on table 1's head/base binaries) have finished -- so the head and base
predictions below are also unmeasured when written.
Instrument: regress/lca_isalane_probe.py, 93 rows = table 3's 77 + session 4f `tailr' (6) + `tailw' (6) + 4h `iir' (4),
frozen by the driver.

WHY: closing pass 2's measuring seat BUILT two 77/77 escapes (regress/artifacts/lcaisalane/opus_c2_20260914/):
t_tails -- the split TAIL cells (len 3/5/6/7 at lane 0) were unrowed because the header said tails start only at the
unmapped port 0x400; they start at every port 0 mod 0x20 (the 8042 at 0x60) -- and x_wfallthru, the write arm's `return'
deleted, which loses IIR_TXRDY on a store to 0x3fa and was never in the header's contract.  Repair 3 ports the seat's
discriminator into the probe, with ONE CHANGE OF MINE (L1, found writing this table's mutants): each `tailw' phase resets
the 8042 command byte to 0x04 before its tail store -- the phases run t7, t6, t5, t3, and without the reset a DECLINED
tail store reads back the previous phase's 0x44 and passes.  d_w6tail below is that change's own kill.

TARGETING: repair 3 ADDS sessions and changes no existing session's commands, so no earlier kill moves; tables 1-3 stand.

CHECKS.  SIBLING PARITY: the tail cells now carry R and W at every tail-only length (3, 5, 6, 7), as the head cells do;
tails of len 1, 2, 4 are the direct lane-0 cells.  CLAIM -> ROW: the header's "at every cell of that space" now includes
the tail cells (4f); the CONTRACT's new x_wfallthru item maps to `iir stb' / `iir stl'.  GUARD vs BODY: the write arm's
`return' routes the forward's result; deleting it keeps `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)' and nulls its routing (clause
(d)'s shape) -- the iir rows store to a port whose READ has a side effect.  CHANNEL (new rows): tailr -- the full
register, a sentinel before each load (a decline keeps it, a mis-placement moves 0x55 one byte); tailw -- the command
byte read back flat after a reset to 0x04 (a decline reads 0x04, a mis-placement 0x21); iir -- IIR & 3 after arming
TXRDY (a phantom read of IIR clears it).

